                <pb facs="0553" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3418: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-25T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 25—8:42
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>183 <hi rendition="#italic">bis</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">199?</hi>].
                    Referring to my cable of July 25th, 1 a.m. Following resignations have been
                    accepted, Ministers of Finance, Justice and Communications. Vice Ministers
                    acting. Also resignation of General Tuan Chih Kuei, Anfu member, commander in
                    chief troops metropolitan district; General Wang, commandant of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">gendarmerie</hi>, to act concurrently. Chihli troops
                    proceeding north on Peking-Kalgan Railway in pursuit of remnant of Tuan’s
                    troops.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
